  "referenceConventions": {
    "geometry": "A fixed gapped SSH lower band with t1=0,t2=1; a declared smooth phase on 30 nonnegative-k selections, explicit conjugation, projection of a derivative, and finite separation versus the differential metric.",
    "order": "Actual Oh actions and six equal-image buckets, normalized C4v Reynolds averages with reciprocal coefficient rescaling, fixed-radius parent-domain field energies, and simultaneous 37-degree coordinate changes.",
    "layer": "Actual cubic-parent-inherited operations on two finite four-layer 001 slabs; unique same-label atom matching, only in-plane periodic wrapping, and an unwrapped finite normal."
  },
  "verification": [
    "Independent mathematics and actual browser_api.run references check the finite cards. Numerical reference outputs use declared tight tolerances while inputs, shapes and metadata remain exact. Source hashes normalize UTF-8 line endings.",
    "Production UI handlers are exercised with iterable non-Array NodeList collections, real native disclosure state, unsubmitted predictions and notes, unfinished ordinary calculator drafts, stale loads and copy completions, invalid scope/fields and explicit manual Run.",
    "The existing quantum-state SPT bridge remains independently mounted. Expert calculation entry does not request the new mathematical cards. English extraction preserves numerical inputs and enums."
  ],
  "boundaries": [
    "These cards implement declared finite examples, not general quantum-geometry, invariant-classification or 80-layer-group solvers. Existing Python tools and their scientific scopes remain authoritative.",
    "The field-energy card compares fixed-radius parent-domain representatives; it does not re-minimize a free energy with an external field. Primed coordinates transform the energy function as well as vectors.",
    "A layer operation absent after marking one surface can still map positions geometrically while failing labels. Normal coordinates are never made periodic.",
    "This release changes no Python computation core or existing catalogue/fixture values. It does not implement the remaining FHS plaquette replay, complete the 197-lesson depth review, expand the reviewed prerequisite graph, certify every scientific workflow or establish student learning gains."
  ],
